1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,180
This star could explode

2
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,350
long after it has stopped shining.

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:06,200
The trigger is not a growing mass.

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,120
It is a falling limit.

5
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:10,250
It’s a black dwarf:

6
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,160
the cold remnant a white dwarf

7
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,380
could become in the far future.

8
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,100
Inside, pressure from electrons

9
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,500
resists gravity.

10
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,820
In a theoretical model,

11
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,320
quantum tunneling allows

12
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,400
extremely slow fusion,

13
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:26,180
gradually making the core

14
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:27,150
richer in iron.

15
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:29,800
That changes how much mass

16
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,100
the remnant can support.

17
00:00:31,721 --> 00:00:33,761
Its mass barely changes.

18
00:00:34,461 --> 00:00:35,511
Its limit falls.

19
00:00:36,421 --> 00:00:38,061
For some of the heaviest remnants,

20
00:00:38,501 --> 00:00:40,461
gravity could finally win:

21
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:41,811
collapse,

22
00:00:42,201 --> 00:00:44,167
and a possible supernova.

23
00:00:44,214 --> 00:00:45,634
The earliest might wait

24
00:00:45,634 --> 00:00:46,994
ten to the power of

25
00:00:46,994 --> 00:00:48,274
eleven hundred years.

26
00:00:48,914 --> 00:00:50,414
But only if protons

27
00:00:50,414 --> 00:00:51,654
don’t decay first.

28
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:53,374
A dead star,

29
00:00:53,374 --> 00:00:57,133
with one more possible ending.
